      "title": "Working with us",
      "description": "Working with us - UOW College Hong Kong Skip to Content We use cookies to improve your experience on our site and to show you personalised advertising. To find out more, read our privacy policy and cookie policy OK, thanks Search Apply now News & Events Students Staff Menu Programmes Show/hide \" Programmes \" menu Programmes Find your programmes Close Bachelor Degrees Higher Diplomas Employees Retraining Board (Chinese only) University of Wollongong Top-up Degrees Diploma in General Studies Applied Learning Associate Degrees Diploma of Applied Education (Chinese only) Admissions Show/hide \" Admissions \" menu Admissions Admission requirements Close Admission requirements International Students How to Apply Direct Application for SSSDP Places Fees and financial assistance About us Show/hide \" About us \" menu About us About us Close Message from the President About the faculties Staff Directory Vision and Mission Campus and facilities Working with us Strategic Plan Commitment to quality Contact us 選擇課程 Show/hide \" 選擇課程 \" menu 選擇課程 課程資訊 Close 學士 高級文憑 ERB僱員再培訓局課程 銜接學士 基礎教育文憑 應用學習 副學士 應用教育文憑課程 申請入學 Show/hide \" 申請入學 \" menu 申請入學 學院課程 Close 入學要求 申請方法 學費、政府資助及獎學金 境外學生 關於我們 Show/hide \" 關於我們 \" menu 關於我們 關於我們 Close 校長的話 學院簡介 教職員名錄 願景及使命 校舍及設施 加入我們團隊 策略計畫 教育質素承諾 聯絡我們 升學資訊 Current Students Staff Apply now News & Events You are here Home Working with us Working with us Current openings Expand All Collapse All Clerical Officer Clerical Officer [Ref.2026NACAD033] UOW College Hong Kong (“UOWCHK”) is an approved post-secondary college registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320).  Being part of the University of Wollongong (UOW) in Australia, our students’ learning experiences are enriched through visits by UOW academics or exchange programmes with UOW and its network universities in Malaysia, Dubai and India. Our wide range of academic programmes include bachelor’s degrees, UOW top-up degrees, sub-degrees, as well as foundation programmes such as Diploma in General Studies, Diploma of Applied Education, and ERB courses. With about 1,600 students, the College attaches high importance to student learning experience. Overseas study tours, mentorship programmes, and internships are organized to prepare our students for the real world. Duties The appointee will provide clerical and front-line counter services in the General Office, assist with handling enquiries from students, staff and the public, perform assigned tasks independently, undertake Saturday duties , and carry out any other duties as assigned. Requirements Applicants must have Level 2 or above in 5 HKDSE subjects including Chinese Language, English Language and Mathematics or 5 passes in HKCEE including Chinese Language, Mathematics and English Language (at least Grade C if syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007) and 2 years’ relevant post-qualification experience. Good communication and interpersonal skills, strong initiative, self-motivated, detail-minded, and high proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Excellent command in MS Excel and strong attention to details with good organizational skills are expected. Good understanding of computer applications including MS Word, PowerPoint and Chinese Word Processing is desirable. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment will normally be made on fixed-term contract for one year. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental schemes. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Social Work, Faculty of Social Sciences Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Social Work, Faculty of Social Sciences [Ref.2026/ACAD032] Faculty of Social Sciences The Faculty of Social Sciences nurtures graduates with strong analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills, cultural sensitivity, a global outlook, and a commitment to lifelong learning. The Faculty offers a range of programmes from diplomas to bachelor’s degrees to prepare students for further study and professional practice. Duties The appointee will undertake teaching and administrative duties for the Bachelor of Social Science in Social Work Programme (full-time and part-time modes). Responsibilities include course development and delivery; coordination of fieldwork (e.g. liaison with placement agencies and oversight of student placements); organisation of pre-placement preparation and other student activities; support for student recruitment; promotion of programme activities; and other duties as assigned by the College. Professorial-grade staff are also expected to engage in research. Requirements Applicants must meet the following requirements: A Master’s degree or preferably a Doctoral degree in Social Work or a related discipline; At least one year of teaching experience in tertiary education; No less than five years of full-time-equivalent Post-degree Professional Practising Experience; and A Registered Social Worker of the Social Workers Registration Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment will normally be made on fixed-term contract for one year. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental schemes. Information and Application Please send an application letter enclosing a curriculum vitae to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The closing date is 09 September 2026 . Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity,  inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment- related purposes. Part-time Lecturers in Logistics, Faculty of Science and Technology Part-time Lecturers in Logistics Faculty of Science and Technology [Ref.2026/ACAD026] Faculty of Science and Technology The Faculty of Science and Technology at UOW College Hong Kong is dedicated to equipping students with the knowledge and skills needed to thrive in today’s fast-evolving technological landscape. Offering a diverse range of programmes—from aviation operations and computer science to environmental and sustainable development—the faculty blends academic rigor with practical training to prepare students for both local and global career opportunities. Students benefit from hands-on learning experiences, an industry-relevant curriculum, and pathways to further studies, including articulation to the University of Wollongong in Australia. With a strong emphasis on innovation, sustainability, and digital transformation, the faculty nurtures future professionals in fields such as logistics, media production, information systems, and emerging technologies like UAVs and generative AI. Whether pursuing a bachelor’s degree, associate degree, or higher diploma, students at the Faculty of Science and Technology are empowered to become forward-thinking contributors to society and industry. We are currently recruiting part-time instructors to support teaching in the EDB Applied Learning (ApL): Logistics (course details at EDB website: https://www.edb.gov.hk/attachment/tc/curriculum-development/cross-kla-studies/applied-learning/course-information/2026-2028/27_Logistics(26-28)_c.pdf ) Duties Appointees are expected to undertake the following tasks: Deliver engaging and practical lessons aligned with curriculum guidelines. Prepare teaching materials and assessments. Support student learning and provide constructive feedback. Participate in occasional meetings or training sessions as required. Requirements Applicants must meet the following requirements: A relevant academic qualification (Master’s degree or above) in the subject area. A minimum of two years’ of teaching experience in post-secondary education and/or relevant industry experience; Strong communication and classroom management skills. Preference will be given to candidates who are available to teach during daytime hours on weekdays. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Part-time Lecturers in Information Technology and Mathematics, Faculty of Science and Technology Part-time Lecturers in Information Technology and Mathematics Faculty of Science and Technology [Ref.2026/ACAD024] Faculty of Science and Technology The Faculty of Science and Technology at UOW College Hong Kong is dedicated to equipping students with the knowledge and skills needed to thrive in today’s fast-evolving technological landscape. Offering a diverse range of programmes—from aviation operations and computer science to environmental and sustainable development—the faculty blends academic rigor with practical training to prepare students for both local and global career opportunities. Students benefit from hands-on learning experiences, an industry-relevant curriculum, and pathways to further studies, including articulation to the University of Wollongong in Australia. With a strong emphasis on innovation, sustainability, and digital transformation, the faculty nurtures future professionals in fields such as logistics, media production, information systems, and emerging technologies like UAVs and generative AI. Whether pursuing a bachelor’s degree, associate degree, or higher diploma, students at the Faculty of Science and Technology are empowered to become forward-thinking contributors to society and industry. We are currently recruiting part-time instructors to support teaching in Associate Degree programmes: Subject areas include: AI Applications and Literacy Programming Game Development Data Communication Theory and Network Administration Mathematics Duties Appointees are expected to undertake the following tasks: Deliver engaging and practical lessons aligned with curriculum guidelines. Prepare teaching materials and assessments. Support student learning and provide constructive feedback. Participate in occasional meetings or training sessions as required. Requirements Applicants must meet the following requirements: A relevant academic qualification (Master’s degree or above) in the subject area. A minimum of two years’ of teaching experience in post-secondary education and/or relevant industry experience; Strong communication and classroom management skills. Preference will be given to candidates who are available to teach during daytime hours on weekdays. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. ERB Instructors ERB Instructors [Ref: 2026/ACAD023] Duties The appointee is expected to deliver various ERB courses at Levels 3 and 4, primarily focused on skill uplifting. This includes preparing course materials, conducting assessments, and providing constructive feedback to students to enhance their learning experience. Requirements All applicants must hold a Degree or Master’s degree in a relevant field, with a minimum of three years of teaching experience, along with relevant working experience in one of the following fields: Project Management : Candidates should have a robust background in managing projects, with a preference for those holding certifications in Agile methodologies or CAPM. A minimum of five years of experience in leading teams, executing projects on time and within budget, and a proven track record of achieving project objectives is essential. Online Business and Marketing : Applicants should demonstrate a strong foundation in digital marketing strategies, with at least three years of experience in online business development and collaboration with key opinion leaders in marketing. Experience in developing and implementing successful marketing campaigns is highly desirable. Financial Services : Instructors should possess significant experience in financial planning and analysis, specifically with a focus on preparation for AFP® certification. Candidates should have at least five years of relevant industry experience, including roles in financial consulting or investment management. Blockchain Development : Candidates must have hands-on experience in blockchain applications, including the development and implementation of blockchain solutions. A minimum of three years of experience in this field, along with a strong understanding of smart contracts and decentralized applications, is required. Data Analysis : Applicants should have practical experience in data analytics, including proficiency in analytical tools and techniques that drive business insights. Candidates should have at least three years of experience in data analysis roles, preferably in a business or technology context. Cloud Computing : Candidates should have substantial experience in cloud technologies, including deployment and management of cloud-based solutions. A minimum of three years of experience in cloud architecture or administration is required. Mobile Application Development : Instructors should have a background in developing Android applications, with experience in both foundational and advanced programming techniques. Candidates should have at least three years of relevant development experience, including familiarity with app deployment and user experience design. Professional English Training : Candidates must have experience in teaching business English, including writing, listening, and speaking skills tailored for professional environments. A minimum of three years of teaching experience in an adult education or corporate training setting is essential. Putonghua Language Training : Instructors should have experience in teaching Putonghua, particularly in business communication contexts. Candidates should have at least three years of teaching experience, with a focus on practical language use in professional settings. Arabic Language Training : Instructors will be responsible for teaching both fundamental and service-related language short courses, each comprising 30 contact hours. Applicants must hold a recognised university degree in Languages, Arts, Translation, English, or a closely related discipline, together with demonstrable experience in teaching the Arabic language. Russian Language Training : Instructors will be responsible for teaching both fundamental and service-related language short courses, each comprising 30 contact hours. Applicants must hold a recognised university degree in Language, Arts, Translation, English, or a closely related discipline, together with demonstrable experience in teaching the Russian language. Arboriculture : Candidates must be ISA Certified Arborists with a minimum of two years of experience in the field. Risk Management (AI Applications) : Instructors will be responsible for delivering the \"Certificate in Risk Management and Decision-Making (AI Applications)\" course, which comprises 30 hours of instruction. Applicants must hold a recognised university degree in Business Administration, Project Management, Risk Management, or a related discipline. Candidates should also possess a PMI® certification (PMI-PMP® or PMI-RMP®) and have a minimum of five years of professional experience in project risk management. This must include practical, hands-on experience in applying artificial intelligence to risk management contexts. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary is based on an hourly rate ranging from $450 to $650, depending on the level of the course, number of participants and the qualifications of the instructor. For specialized professional courses that have specific instructor requirements, such as project management, the hourly rate may reach up to $1,000, subject to the instructor's expertise and the course's complexity. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Part-time Lecturers in  UAV and Low-Altitude Economy, Faculty of Science and Technology Part-time Lecturers in  UAV and Low-Altitude Economy Faculty of Science and Technology [Ref.2026/ACAD017] The Faculty of Science and Technology at UOW College Hong Kong is dedicated to equipping students with the knowledge and skills needed to thrive in today’s fast-evolving technological landscape. Offering a diverse range of programmes—from aviation operations and computer science to environmental and sustainable development—the faculty blends academic rigor with practical training to prepare students for both local and global career opportunities. Students benefit from hands-on learning experiences, an industry-relevant curriculum, and pathways to further studies, including articulation to the University of Wollongong in Australia. With a strong emphasis on innovation, sustainability, and digital transformation, the faculty nurtures future professionals in fields such as logistics, media production, information systems, and emerging technologies like UAVs and generative AI. Whether pursuing a bachelor’s degree, associate degree, or higher diploma, students at the Faculty of Science and Technology are empowered to become forward-thinking contributors to society and industry. We are currently recruiting part-time instructors to support teaching in the EDB Applied Learning (ApL): UAV and Low-Altitude Economy (course details at EDB website: https://www.edb.gov.hk/attachment/tc/curriculum-development/cross-kla-studies/applied-learning/course-information/2026-2028/56_UAV%20&%20Low-altitude%20Econ(26-28)_c.pdf ) Duties Appointees are expected to undertake the following tasks: Deliver engaging and practical lessons aligned with curriculum guidelines. Prepare teaching materials and assessments. Support student learning and provide constructive feedback. Participate in occasional meetings or training sessions as required. Requirements Applicants must meet the following requirements: A relevant academic qualification (Master’s degree or above) in the subject area. A minimum of two years’ of teaching experience in post-secondary education and/or relevant industry experience; Strong communication and classroom management skills. Preference will be given to candidates who are available to teach during daytime hours on weekdays. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Please submit Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Part-time Lecturers in  KOL Marketing and Generative AI, Faculty of Science and Technology Part-time Lecturers in  KOL Marketing and Generative AI Faculty of Science and Technology [Ref.2026/ACAD018] The Faculty of Science and Technology at UOW College Hong Kong is dedicated to equipping students with the knowledge and skills needed to thrive in today’s fast-evolving technological landscape. Offering a diverse range of programmes—from aviation operations and computer science to environmental and sustainable development—the faculty blends academic rigor with practical training to prepare students for both local and global career opportunities. Students benefit from hands-on learning experiences, an industry-relevant curriculum, and pathways to further studies, including articulation to the University of Wollongong in Australia. With a strong emphasis on innovation, sustainability, and digital transformation, the faculty nurtures future professionals in fields such as logistics, media production, information systems, and emerging technologies like UAVs and generative AI. Whether pursuing a bachelor’s degree, associate degree, or higher diploma, students at the Faculty of Science and Technology are empowered to become forward-thinking contributors to society and industry. We are currently recruiting part-time instructors to support teaching in the EDB Applied Learning (ApL): KOL Marketing and Generative AI (course details at EDB website: https://www.edb.gov.hk/attachment/tc/curriculum-development/cross-kla-studies/applied-learning/course-information/2026-2028/23_AI%20in%20Biz%20Data(26-28)_c.pdf ) Duties Appointees are expected to undertake the following tasks: Deliver engaging and practical lessons aligned with curriculum guidelines. Prepare teaching materials and assessments. Support student learning and provide constructive feedback. Participate in occasional meetings or training sessions as required. Requirements Applicants must meet the following requirements: A relevant academic qualification (Master’s degree or above) in the subject area. A minimum of two years’ of teaching experience in post-secondary education and/or relevant industry experience; Strong communication and classroom management skills. Preference will be given to candidates who are available to teach during daytime hours on weekdays. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Please submit Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Executive Officers Executive Officers [Ref. 2026NACAD001] UOW College Hong Kong (“UOWCHK”) is an approved post-secondary college registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320).  Being part of the University of Wollongong (UOW) in Australia, our students’ learning experiences are enriched through visits by UOW academics or exchange programmes with UOW and its network universities in Malaysia, Dubai and India. Our wide range of academic programmes include bachelor’s degrees, UOW top-up degrees, sub-degrees, as well as foundation programmes such as Diploma in General Studies, Diploma of Applied Education, and ERB courses. With about 1,600 students, the College attaches high importance to student learning experience. Overseas study tours, mentorship programmes, and internships are organized to prepare our students for the real world. Duties The appointee will be responsible for (a) managing the operation of the General Office and supervising supporting staff; (b) performing various administrative functions; (c) assisting in programme admission and registration; and (d) performing other duties as assigned. Requirements Applicants must have a good honours degree and 2 years’ relevant post-qualification experience. A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, proficiency in computer applications, good interpersonal and organization skills, and strong initiative are required. The appointee should be well-organized, flexible, adaptable, and able to work independently. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a written test. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment will normally be made on fixed-term contract for one year. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental schemes. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Clerical Officers Clerical Officers [Ref.2026NACAD013] Duties The appointee is expected to provide clerical support to the Faculty Office, perform tasks independently, handle general enquiries and perform any other duties as assigned. Requirements Applicants must have Level 2 or above in 5 HKDSE subjects including Chinese Language, English Language and Mathematics or 5 passes in HKCEE including Chinese Language, Mathematics and English Language (at least Grade C if syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007) and 2 years’ relevant post-qualification experience. Good communication and interpersonal skills, strong initiative, self-motivated, detail-minded, and high proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Excellent command in MS Excel and strong attention to details with good organizational skills are expected. Good understanding of computer applications including MS Word, PowerPoint and Chinese Word Processing is desirable. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment will normally be made on fixed-term contract for one year. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental schemes. Information and Application Please submit a Cover Letter together with a Curriculum Vitae and a completed Application Form to UOWCHK, c/o Human Resources Unit, UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, N.T., Hong Kong or by Email: uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au . The Application Form is available for download under “Job Applications” on our website. Please note that applications submitted without a complete Application Form will not be processed . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please quote the reference number in the application. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. UOWCHK is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to the principles of diversity, inclusiveness and equality. Personal data provided by applicants will be used strictly in accordance with UOWCHK’s personal data policy and for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. General information Expand All Collapse All About UOW College Hong Kong UOW College Hong Kong is registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320) in Hong Kong.  We are part of the University of Wollongong (UOW) global network in Dubai, Malaysia and Australia with about 1,200 students.  We offer a wide range of Degree, Top-up Degree, Associate Degree(AD) and Higher Diploma(HD) programmes, Diploma in General Studies (DipGS), and the Diploma of Applied Education.  All academic programmes of the College are locally accredited, quality-assured, and recognized under the Qualifications Framework. With about 150 well-qualified and dedicated staff, we are highly regarded for our committed teaching focus, rigor in quality assurance and emphasis on the whole-person development of students.  The College’s campus in Tai Wai is easily accessible from a nearby MTR station and other public transport.  For more details about the College, please visit https://www.uowchk.edu.hk . Notes to Applicants The information provided in your application will be used for appointment to the UOW College Hong Kong and other employment-related purposes. It may be disclosed to personnel, faculties or agencies authorised to process the information for purposes relating to appointment e.g. education, qualifications and health assessments. Information provided by unsuccessful candidates will be destroyed after the exercise when no longer required. The UOW College Hong Kong undertakes, in its data management policies and practices, to observe the spirit of the data protection principles and to comply with the requirements of the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance of Hong Kong. For correction of or access to personal data after submission of the application, please contact the subject officer of the Human Resources Unit and quote the reference of the post applied for. The College is committed to the principle and practice of non-discrimination in the fulfilment of its dual responsibilities as an employer and a provider of higher education. It considers that talents, skills, intelligence, ambition and potential required by the College of its staff and students are spread across the community and can be found in people irrespective of their race and national origin, sex and gender identity, sexual orientation, abilities and disabilities, age, religion and family status. With the aim of securing the best qualified persons for the study programmes and jobs it offers, the College undertakes to provide equal access, consideration, encouragement and support in all areas of its student and staff recruitment and management. Decisions are made on the basis of merits measured against criteria which are directly related to the work/study place; these criteria are objective and can be readily assessed, including qualifications, knowledge and skills, experience and personal qualities. Job Applications Applicants are requested to quote the reference number of the post applied for in their application. Please submit a curriculum vitae * together with a completed application form to the Human Resources Unit on or before the closing date. You can download the application form from the link below: Application Form for Academic/Non-Academic Full Time Positions Application Form for Academic/Non-Academic Part-time/ Temporary Positions * Applications for academic positions should include the following information in the curriculum vitae, where applicable: Academic and Professional Qualifications Chronological Employment History Teaching Record Research/ Applied Work Achievements Publication List Referees (as specified in the advertisement) Community and Professional Service By Email By Post uowchk-hr@uow.edu.au c/o Human Resources Unit UOW College Hong Kong 3/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, New Territories, Hong Kong Human Resources Office Location Scroll to Top Services and help Services and help Current students Study at UOWCHK What to study How to apply Faculties Faculties Arts and Humanities Business Science and Technology Social Sciences UOW entities UOW entities UOW Australia UOW College Australia UOW in Dubai UOW Global Enterprises UOW Malaysia Connect with us Connect with us Contact us How to Apply Admission Info UOW College Hong Kong, 1/F, 18 Che Kung Miu Road, Tai Wai, New Territories, Hong Kong (accessible via MTR Tai Wai Station Exit B) Phone: 2707 3111 Email: uowchk-main@uow.edu.au UOW College Hong Kong is an organisation that supports, embraces and celebrates diverse cultures. Copyright © 2026 University of Wollongong CRICOS Provider No: 00102E | TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12062 | ABN: 61 060 567 686 Privacy & cookie usage | Copyright & disclaimer Close Search"
